==== OEM firmware backdoor ====

Some EnGenius devices have a backdoor built in to drop from their limited CLI into a root shell. More information can be found in [[https://gist.github.com/darconeous/b24cdaa853a8f35162f2f8e3a3050149|this gist]], but in this section there will be instructions to install OpenWRT.

First make sure that telnet is enabled. This can be done on the Web UI under the "Management" section and then specifically the "Advanced" page. On the same page, enable SSH, this is not relevant for now, but will be needed later.

After that, connect to the device using telnet. Then login using the credentials that work on the Web UI. You will be dropped into a command prompt that looks somewhat like the following:
<code>
*** Hi admin, welcome to use cli(V-1.9.11) ***
---========= Commands Help =========---
      stat -- Status
       sys -- System
    wless2 -- 2.4G-Wireless
    wless5 -- 5G-Wireless
      mgmt -- Management
      tree -- Tree
      help -- Help
    reboot -- Reboot
    logout -- Logout
ecb1750>
</code>

At this point insert the string "1d68d24ea0d9bb6e19949676058f1b93" and press enter. After that "ecb1750>" turns into ">". Then execute the command "login". Ater that you will be dropped into the root shell for the OEM firmware:
<code>
