Then change the password using the "passwd" command.

At this point it should be possible to connect over ssh, but at the time of writing (2024-06) the default OpenSSH package in many distro's will not support the outdated algorithms the older Dropbear version uses by default. To remedy this you can add "-oKexAlgorithms=+diffie-hellman-group1-sha1 -oHostKeyAlgorithms=+ssh-dss -oPubkeyAcceptedAlgorithms=+ssh-dss" to the ssh command you execute to connect to the device.

This will still drop you into the CLI program. The next step is to remove this automatic invocation. For this you can use vim to edit the dropbear service at "/etc/init.d/dropbear" and remove the part that invokes the CLI program. This will turn the following snippet from:
<code>
[...]
# l) login path
    cli_enable="$(uci get cfg_cli.@cli[0].cli_enable)" 2>/dev/null
    [ "${cli_enable}" -eq 1 ] && append args "-l ${PROG_CLI}"
        # C) banner file
        config_get val "${section}" BannerFile
        [ -f "${val}" ] && append args "-b ${val}"
[...]
</code>

Into:
<code>
[...]
# l) login path
    cli_enable="$(uci get cfg_cli.@cli[0].cli_enable)" 2>/dev/null
    [ "${cli_enable}" -eq 1 ]
        # C) banner file
        config_get val "${section}" BannerFile
        [ -f "${val}" ] && append args "-b ${val}"
[...]
</code>

After restarting dropbear using "/etc/init.d/dropbear restart" ssh will accept the password you set earlier.

At that point it's possible to copy over the sysupgrade bin you fetch from the firmware selector. When using "scp", be sure to add the key algorithm flags from earlier and to add the "-O" (dash Capital O) flag to make scp use legacy methods to copy over the file:
<code>
$ scp -r -O -oKexAlgorithms=+diffie-hellman-group1-sha1 -oHostKeyAlgorithms=+ssh-dss -oPubkeyAcceptedAlgorithms=+ssh-dss openwrt-23.05.3-ath79-generic-engenius_ecb1750-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin root@192.168.1.1:/tmp/openwrt.bin
